@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] brady-secret-free-diagnostics
Brady diagnostics MUST emit only closed, validated event fields. Raw URLs,
headers, bodies, certificates, keys, peer error text and arbitrary process state
MUST NOT reach logs, including runtime crash reports.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] brady-public-cache-only
Only complete explicitly public responses, or responses satisfying the reviewed
public commit-pinned GitHub archive policy, to eligible anonymous GET requests
MUST enter shared storage. Credentials, cookies, signed URLs and ambiguous
cache policy MUST bypass storage and reuse.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:capacity] brady-disposable-bounded-cache
Cached objects and in-progress writes MUST share a bounded budget. Cache storage
failure MUST preserve proxied streaming where possible, without permitting a
direct guest bypass. Unconfirmed deletion MUST NOT count as reclaimed space.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] brady-native-evidence
Unit and property tests MUST NOT establish physical interception, TLS trust,
ZFS behavior or Firecracker isolation; native acceptance MUST verify those paths.
